# Theme toggle

An icon button cycling the colour theme: system → light → dark.

<%= embed :theme_toggle, :default %>

## When to use

- Once, in the header — it ships there already. Pages never need to
  render it themselves.

## When not to use

- Anywhere a second instance would appear; one global control.
- For any other cycling control — its Stimulus controller is
  theme-specific, not a generic toggle.

## Usage

`render_theme_toggle` (`Gesso::Components::ThemeToggleHelper`) — no params. A
ghost icon button whose Stimulus `theme` controller swaps the
monitor / sun / moon icon to match the active mode and persists the
choice. This atomic component is built inline in the helper; it has no
partial.

```erb
<%%= render_theme_toggle %>
```

## Do and don't

- Do leave "system" as the default experience; the toggle is an
  override, not a setting users must find.
- Do test state-colour-heavy pages in both themes — the toggle is
  the quickest way (see the *Colour* foundations page).
- Don't add theme-conditional markup to pages; theming is tokens in
  CSS, never logic in views.

## Accessibility and content

- Carries `aria-label="Toggle theme"` — the icon-only button stays
  named for assistive tech.
- Keyboard operable as a plain `<button>`; one press per cycle step.
